  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &#x2018;&#x2018;Supporting Women and Girls in Ethiopia&apos;s lowlands to realize their rights, and live healthy and productive lives&#x2019;&#x2019; project in Ethiopia, implemented by The Save the Children, aims to contribute towards greater voice, protection and economic empowerment of women and girls in Somali and Afar regions. The project directly benefits over 42,000 people, 70% of whom are women and girls.  Activities include (i) empowering adolescent girls and young women economically and socially (ii) publicly advocacy for gender rights (iii) reducing practice of negative gender practices including FGM and early marriage (iv) strengthening systems and mechanisms that protect the rights of girls and women.</narrative>
  </description>
